# A reference struct's emitted C layout already carries a `header` member (the
# reference-count header), so a user field of that name produced TWO members
# with one name — "duplicate member 'header'" — and every `p.header` access
# silently resolved to the RC header instead, cascading into incompatible-type
# errors at the constructor, the traversal function and each use site. It
# type-checked cleanly, so the only symptom was a wall of C errors naming
# generated temps.
#
# This case pins the REJECTION: `check` must fail with the reserved-field
# diagnostic, at the field's own source location. stdout_keep_match asserts THE
# error rather than merely A failure — a case that only checked rc would pass on
# any unrelated breakage.
# issues/fixed/ref-struct-field-named-header-collides-with-rc-header.md
stdout_keep_match="header" is a reserved field name in a reference struct
timeout=120
